1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,200
Your config file. Everyone with repo access has all of them.

2
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:05,000
Secrets, keys and certificates. Three kinds, one place.

3
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:07,800
The credential that opens the vault. You moved the problem.

4
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:10,600
A secret to get the secrets. It leaks the same way, and it expires.

5
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:13,400
Azure issues it. Nothing is stored, so nothing can be stolen.

6
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:16,200
The app may read. Your laptop may not. That is an RBAC role.

7
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:19,000
And the audit log says who read which secret, and when.

8
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:21,800
The vault holds them. The identity opens it. Nothing is written down.
